#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
FEDERAL BANK DOCUMENT AI - Optimized Aadhaar masking for account-opening PDFs

Engines:
    - PyMuPDF
    - PaddleOCR
    - OpenCV
    - RF-DETR

Supported data:
    1. Printed/typed Aadhaar numbers in the PDF/page.
    2. Aadhaar cards embedded in or photographed on the page.
    3. QR codes associated with detected Aadhaar cards.

NOT supported:
    - Handwritten Aadhaar numbers.

Masking rule:
    1234 5678 9012  ->  XXXX XXXX 9012

Security:
    - Full Aadhaar numbers are never printed to logs.
    - A 12-digit number is masked only after Verhoeff validation.
    - Last four digits remain visible.

Major performance changes:
    - Native PDF text layer is checked before PaddleOCR.
    - Page-level RF-DETR runs once by default, not at 0/90/180/270 degrees.
    - Rotations are used only for embedded-image regions.
    - PaddleOCR card-number verification stops after a valid upright read.
    - Whole-page QR decoding is removed from the RF-DETR path.
    - RF-DETR tiling is adaptive and configurable.
    - No handwriting/OpenCV connected-component pipeline.
    - Optional per-stage profiling.
    - Reduced image copying and unnecessary rotations.

Examples:
    python main_optimized.py input/fedtest.pdf
    python main_optimized.py input/fedtest.pdf --debug
    python main_optimized.py input/fedtest.pdf --tile 0
    python main_optimized.py input/fedtest.pdf --profile
    python main_optimized.py --no-model input/fedtest.pdf
"""

